Data   : the web page reads NO API — it renders from the current `location.pathname` (navigation/local state) and a
         Levenshtein ranking of the closest known routes (web closestRoute.ts over routeRegistry.ts). This port mirrors
         that exactly: NotFoundPageModel.kt ports the two-row `levenshtein` + `closestRoutes` (distance vs BOTH the
         path and the label, cap <=6, top 5) and projects the suggestion candidates from the app's own canonical
         `io.teslasync.android.navigation.Destinations` table — the native single-source-of-truth that mirrors
         web/src/App.tsx, the same role the web ROUTE_REGISTRY plays — excluding parameterized routes (web `if
         (r.hidden) continue`: they cannot be navigated to without an argument) and the not-found route itself.
         NotFoundPageViewModel projects buildNotFoundSnapshot(attemptedPath) through the shared cache-then-network
         Resource -> UiState pipeline (Resource.Success) so the stateless screen renders through the same data-state
         contract every parity page uses. No HTTP, no store. refresh()/retry() re-derive.
Path   : the attempted/unmatched URL (web `location.pathname`) is threaded from the nav back-stack entry's optional
         `path` argument when a caller supplies one; absent that, the model falls back to the canonical not-found path
         ("/not-found") so the body always reads naturally. The suggestion engine is wired + real either way (a path
         with close matches surfaces them; an unmatched path with nothing within edit-distance 6 yields no block,
         exactly as the web hides the section on `suggestions.length === 0`). Documented here, not silent (Covenant #9).
Strings: every one of the 7 manifest keys (notFound.body/didYouMean/goBack/goHome/heading/openSearch/title) already
         exists in the generated platform catalog as `translation_notFound_*` (res/values{,-ar,-he}/strings.xml) — they
         are reused verbatim (no new keys added; notFound.body keeps its `%1$s` path placeholder). Every visible literal
         resolves via stringResource(R.string.translation_notFound_*); zero hardcoded text.
Nav    : Destinations 'notFound' -> /not-found pre-existing (Destinations.kt:184; metadata-only). Host wired via
         PageHosts.register(notFound){ NotFoundRoute() }, upgrading the route from the shared bare NotFoundScreen to the
         full web-parity GlassPanel surface. The shared NotFoundScreen is intentionally retained as the unhosted-
         destination fallback (NavigationShellTest asserts it), so the else-branch in TeslaSyncNavHost is untouched.
         Forward navigation uses the shared DeepLinkRouter (teslasync://app/...) — the sanctioned page-host seam, no
         LocalNavController is exposed (ExplorePage/GlancePage precedent): Go-to-dashboard -> "/", suggestions ->
         their path, Open-command-palette -> "/search" (the same target the chrome's search action opens, AppScaffold
         onSearch — the native analogue of the web command palette). Go-back uses the back dispatcher (web
         window.history.back()).

